    <selectionEntryGroup name="Psychic Powers" id="303f-8d77-2f63-62c9" collapsible="true" collective="false" hidden="false" import="true">
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="0801-108a-fbb5-e6eb" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
      </constraints>
      <modifiers>
        <modifier field="0801-108a-fbb5-e6eb" type="increment" value="1">
          <repeats>
            <repeat childId="e0d3-739a-9026-4668" childName="The Familiar" field="selections" repeats="1" roundUp="false" scope="parent" shared="true" value="1"/>
          </repeats>
        </modifier>
      </modifiers>
      <selectionEntries>
        <selectionEntry name="Emperor&apos;s Guidance" id="859a-a644-05e5-af24" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="0b34-a94b-951e-8f33" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="30"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Emperor&apos;s Guidance" id="8792-79fb-f2a3-7313" hidden="false">
              <description>This psychic power is used at the start of the Alien Hunter turn. Nominate one friendly unit with a model within 6” of the Inquisitor (which may be the Inquisitor‘s own unit). This unit may re-roll any missed shooting to hit rolls until the start of the next Alien Hunter turn. If the unit is using a guess range weapon you may re-roll the Scatter dice if
a “hit” is not scored with the first roll.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Hammerhand" id="a252-e261-452d-95e4" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="a4ae-0e64-2b5e-6c58" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="10"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Hammerhand" id="2059-27ca-5ec7-fad3" hidden="false">
              <description>This psykic power may be used at the beginning of any Assault phase. On a successful psychic test the psyker doubles their Strength until their next turn. The psyker also counts as having an additional close combat weapon. They may not benefit from any power weapons or other special close combat attacks while this power is active.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="His Will Be Done" id="1c55-a781-e9f5-0b9d" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="b729-9ac1-c030-bb32" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="15"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="His Will Be Done" id="04e0-6dcc-c6cf-33d1" hidden="false">
              <description>His Will Be Done is a psychic power that may be used in the Assault phase, before the Inquisitor has made any attacks. Every unsaved wound inflicted by the Inquisitor counts as two for the purposes of determining which side has won the assault.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Scourging" id="c1bd-8802-edec-da8c" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="8570-7fc8-7e3f-8529" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="20"/>
          </costs>
          <profiles>
            <profile name="Scourging" id="85fc-7ad1-3485-f486" hidden="false" typeId="b399-8a1b-bf0b-c5b7" typeName="Weapon">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Range" typeId="deb8-131d-bdcf-1376">18&quot;</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="S" typeId="24d8-2110-08fa-d844">5</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="AP" typeId="25ce-028f-0aae-2855">5</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Type" typeId="d3f6-19e8-ac9e-ae13">Assault D6</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Abilities" typeId="492d-1f80-b777-26f2">Ignore invulnerable saves</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Scourging" id="7578-97fb-85e1-c14d" hidden="false">
              <description>Scourging is a psychic power that may be used in the Psykers Shooting phase instead of firing a weapon. Roll to hit, wound and save as normal invulnerable saves may not be taken against wounds caused by Scourging.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Psychic Communion" id="4f02-3610-f225-c4cb" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="51d2-3e73-5bae-421e" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="15"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Psychic Communion" id="9761-f123-75ae-4cbc" hidden="false">
              <description>Psychic Communion is used at the start of the Movement phase before reserve rolls are made. If successful, you may re-roll the Scatter die of any units that Deep Strike during this phase. </description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Psychic Invasion" id="fd38-8695-8c25-567c" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="8b01-607c-7787-6139" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="15"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Psychic Invasion" id="b44d-adc7-ed48-1bdb" hidden="false">
              <description>The power is used in the Shooting phase instead of firing a weapon, has a range of 12“ and requires line of sight. The unit must pass a Leadership test; if they fail they are pinned until the start of the next Alien Hunter turn. The
power has no effect on models with no Leadership rating or which are immune to pinning. 


The main effect of this spell is far greater though. While they are psychically assaulted the Inquisitor pulls information from the targets’ minds. Each time the Inquisitor successfully pins a unit with the Psychic Invasion it will earn 50 Victory Points for its side in missions using the Victory Points special rule. This Victory Point bonus can only be earned once per enemy unit per game.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
        <selectionEntry name="Word of the Emperor" id="6dc5-940f-c558-a5f7" hidden="false" import="true" type="upgrade">
          <constraints>
            <constraint id="aa2b-50e9-d489-674a" field="selections" includeChildForces="false" includeChildSelections="false" percentValue="false" scope="parent" shared="true" type="max" value="1"/>
          </constraints>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="4ed5-2f92-9abc-2870" value="10"/>
          </costs>
          <rules>
            <rule name="Word of the Emperor" id="297b-fd48-d166-8e85" hidden="false">
              <description>This power can be used at the beginning of the enemy Assault phase, even if the psyker is engaged in close combat. All enemy units attempting to charge the psyker or his unit must pass a Leadership test. On a failure they may not assault that turn.</description>
            </rule>
          </rules>
        </selectionEntry>
      </selectionEntries>
    </selectionEntryGroup>
